@node Overview
@chapter Overview

Protean's inbox shows@comma{} beside the line at point@comma{} the task above and the message it is about below (Protean's manual@comma{} ``The preview''). Protean names no client: it asks the functions of @code{protean-message-open-functions} to open the message. @samp{protean-extras.el} provides one such function per channel I read in Emacs@comma{} each of which prepares its client's buffer at the message and hands it to Protean without displaying anything itself. With the buffer each gives where the message is in it@comma{} so that the preview marks it: the Slack message's @samp{ts}@comma{} the Signal message's @samp{sgn-message-rowid}@comma{} telega's button of the message. An email is its buffer alone and needs no mark.

@multitable {aaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa}
@headitem Channel
@tab Function
@tab Client
@item email
@tab @code{protean-extras-open-email}
@tab mu4e's renderer@comma{} in a buffer of its own
@item Slack
@tab @code{protean-extras-open-slack}
@tab emacs-slack@comma{} the room or the thread
@item Signal
@tab @code{protean-extras-open-signal}
@tab sgn (@code{sgn-message-buffer})
@item Telegram
@tab @code{protean-extras-open-telegram}
@tab telega
@item WhatsApp
@tab @code{protean-extras-open-whatsapp}
@tab wsp (@code{wsp-message-buffer})
@end multitable

@code{protean-extras-openers} lists the five@comma{} for @code{protean-message-open-functions}.

The same clients take a task's draft as a reply@comma{} for Protean's @samp{R} (Protean's manual@comma{} ``Replying in the client''); see @ref{Replies, , Replies}.

@node Email
@chapter Email

@findex protean-extras-open-email
@code{protean-extras-open-email} finds the message by its Message-ID with @samp{mu find}@comma{} and renders its file in @samp{*Protean mail*} with mu4e's own renderer@comma{} in @code{mu4e-view-mode}@comma{} so that it reads as in mu4e. mu4e's view and headers buffers are left as they are@comma{} and the message's flags are not changed. A Message-ID mu does not know is an error@comma{} which Protean shows as the reason for its own view.

@node Slack
@chapter Slack

@findex protean-extras-open-slack
@vindex protean-extras-slack-teams
@code{protean-extras-open-slack} opens the message's room at it@comma{} or@comma{} for a reply in a thread@comma{} the thread@comma{} and hands over the buffer once the message is loaded. The team is the one @code{protean-extras-slack-teams} names for the message's Protean account@comma{} an alist of (ACCOUNT . TEAM-NAME); it must be registered and connected. An account with no team@comma{} a team not connected and a room emacs-slack does not know are errors.

@node Signal and Telegram
@chapter Signal and Telegram

@findex protean-extras-open-signal
@findex protean-extras-open-telegram
@code{protean-extras-open-signal} hands over sgn's chat buffer at the message (@code{sgn-message-buffer}). @code{protean-extras-open-telegram} hands over telega's chat buffer once telega has gone to the message; Telegram must be running.

@node WhatsApp
@chapter WhatsApp

@findex protean-extras-open-whatsapp
@code{protean-extras-open-whatsapp} hands over wsp's chat buffer at the message (@code{wsp-message-buffer})@comma{} and marks the message by its @samp{wsp-id}. A message wa-archive's store does not hold is an error@comma{} with wsp's reason.

@node Replies
@chapter Replies

@findex protean-extras-stage-email
@findex protean-extras-stage-slack
@findex protean-extras-stage-signal
@findex protean-extras-stage-telegram
@findex protean-extras-stage-whatsapp
@vindex protean-extras-stagers
Protean's @samp{R} puts a task's draft in its message's client@comma{} as a reply that you send@comma{} through @code{protean-message-stage-functions}. @code{protean-extras-stagers} lists one stager per channel:

@multitable {aaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa}
@headitem Channel
@tab Function
@tab Where the draft waits
@item email
@tab @code{protean-extras-stage-email}
@tab a reply in mu4e (@code{mu4e-compose-reply}@comma{} org-msg's buffer when it composes)@comma{} above the quote
@item Slack
@tab @code{protean-extras-stage-slack}
@tab emacs-slack's compose buffer of the thread@comma{} or of the room
@item Signal
@tab @code{protean-extras-stage-signal}
@tab sgn's input@comma{} replying to the message
@item Telegram
@tab @code{protean-extras-stage-telegram}
@tab telega's input@comma{} replying to the message
@item WhatsApp
@tab @code{protean-extras-stage-whatsapp}
@tab wsp's input@comma{} replying to the message
@end multitable

Each opens the message as its opener does@comma{} then starts a reply to it. A Slack message in a thread is answered in the thread@comma{} any other in its room. Nothing is sent. When the reply box already holds text@comma{} the stager leaves it as it is and says so. sgn and wsp send no typing indicator for the draft; they do when you type.

